      // Found 2026-09-25 auditing the grandfather program: this object is built
      // FRESH here (it swaps in a just-fetched `plan`/`gamePlan`), unlike every
      // other renewalCharge caller (worker/billing.ts's sweep, the saved-card
      // path in lib/actions-payment-method.ts, the dashboard's own spend figures)
      // which all pass the raw Server row straight through and so carry these two
      // optional fields for free. This literal had silently dropped BOTH — a
      // real production server can (and, checked live, several do) carry a
      // `grandfatheredRenewalCents` that no longer matches its live plan/game-plan
      // price, and every one of them would have been charged the LIVE (possibly
      // raised) price the moment its owner clicked "Renew now" themselves,
      // instead of the frozen rate the automatic sweep would have honored —
      // exactly the "renews at that price forever, independent of the live
      // catalog" promise this field exists to keep. Same failure shape as the two
      // incidents lib/renewal-quote.ts's own docstring warns about: not a wrong
      // formula, a caller that quietly fed the right one incomplete inputs.
